      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "You could ask the cluster for a single pod, and it would run."
        },
        {
          "text": "But if that pod's node fails, the pod is simply gone."
        },
        {
          "text": "So you almost never create pods yourself. You create a Deployment."
        },
        {
          "text": "The Deployment creates a ReplicaSet, whose only job is keeping the right number of pods running."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the ReplicaSet creates the pods: two of them, because we'll ask for two."
        },
        {
          "text": "Each layer is a controller running the loop from Episode 0: compare what you asked for with what's running, and close the gap.",
          "senses": {
            "close": "verb"
          },
          "pauseAfter": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
