          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            27,
            32
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The app reads its settings from a ConfigMap called golinks-config.",
          "say": "The app reads its settings from a ConfigMap called golinks config."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the database password comes from a Secret. Episode 3 opens up both.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "probes",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/golinks-deployment.yaml",
      "range": [
        33,
        56
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            35,
            40
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            42,
            48
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            50,
            56
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Next come three health checks, called probes. The startup probe gives the app up to a minute to start, and holds off the other two until it has.",
          "senses": {
            "minute": "time"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The liveness probe asks whether the process is still healthy. If it fails three times in a row, the kubelet restarts the container."
        },
        {
          "text": "The readiness probe asks whether the pod can serve requests right now, database included. If not, it stops getting traffic, but it isn't restarted."
        },
        {
          "text": "Episode 6 covers all three in depth, once there's a database and a Service to test them against.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "resources",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/golinks-deployment.yaml",
      "range": [
        49,
        62
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            58,
            60
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            61,
            62
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Last, resources. Requests are what the pod is promised: a tenth of a CPU core, and 64 mebibytes of memory."
        },
        {
          "text": "The limit is a ceiling. If the app ever takes more than 128 mebibytes, it's killed and restarted."
        },
        {
          "text": "We leave out a CPU limit on purpose. Hitting one slows the app down instead of stopping it, which is much harder to notice.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
